& [MultiAuthorityRevision] is explicit
  + phase3_evidence was governed by the Phase3 Strict Pure Machine Forms source and signature
  + topology_forms was governed by the Phase3 Topology Machine Forms and receipt root-binding revision sources and replacement signature
  + scanner and seal formations use the old term but grant no implementation authority
  + the new source must preserve exact predecessor artifacts and declare which signatures are superseded for the changed machine meaning
  + unchanged prior behavior outside the selected delta remains inherited, not reauthored
  + one canonical revision may coordinate the cross-module vocabulary only if every affected authority and artifact hash is bound

& [SJSRequiredStages] are complete before code
  + source preservation
  + SJS input audit across every affected authority
  + delineation and exploded atomic requirements
  + semantic refinement of evidence, observation, state, issuer, and consumer roles
  + constraint ledger and post-artifact reapplication
  + pruning and growth disposition
  + seven-fold identity, language, provenance, ownership, fault, effect, and evolution exhaustion
  + data design for types, fields, relations, versions, lineage, states, and representations
  + justification, implementation plan, registry, requirement matrix, build slice, phase lock, canonical revision, and replacement satisfaction signatures
  + SJS artifact binding guard with exact paths, bytes, hashes, and prerequisite signatures

& [Effects] are zero
  + no unsafe
  + no Windows API
  + no filesystem observation or mutation in production
  + no process, environment, clock, random, network, persistence, database, Git runtime, model, tool, or FPGA operation
  + no physical fixture, topology scan, acquisition, receipt issuance, admission, mutation, seal, test-execution effect, cleanup, or promotion

& [StopConditions] are mandatory
  + stop if quiescent remains in the new public machine meaning
  + stop if the old field, enum, token, or profiles decode successfully
  + stop if supplied pair Equal is accepted as repeated physical evidence
  + stop if OsSnapshotProven is admitted without new provenance fields and authority
  + stop if unchanged scanner profile is treated as scanner implementation authority
  + stop if a new dependency, unsafe block, platform call, effect, migration shim, default, alias, or public constructor broadening appears
  + stop if any predecessor source is overwritten
  + stop if an affected authority is omitted from the SJS input manifest
  + stop on stale evidence or failed verification

& [Rollback] is exact
  + before implementation, remove only derived revision artifacts and retain this raw source
  + after implementation, restore the two modules and their tests to the pre-revision commit and remove revision closure artifacts
  + no database migration, physical cleanup, receipt invalidation job, or external coordination is needed because no producer or persisted consumer exists

& [SourceBoundary] is non-authorizing
  + this document records selected intent
  + it does not supersede predecessor signatures by itself
  + it does not authorize implementation
  + it does not authorize physical execution
  + only complete SJS, explicit supersession, artifact-bound replacement signatures, implementation proof, and publication can change those states
